<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugen Leviné</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugen Leviné was a Russian-born German Communist who took over the Bavarian Soviet Republic in April 1919, a week after its proclamation, and formed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a>. His government decreed the socialisation of banks and industry before government troops and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freikorps">Freikorps</a> crushed it in early May. Leviné was tried for high treason and shot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> in June 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eugen-levine.jpg" alt="Eugen Leviné" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eugen_Levin%C3%A9_circa_1919_Crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
